# The `-M` option is not POSIX-compliant, so we need to handle it differently.
# The `-N` option is not POSIX-compliant, so we need to handle it differently.
# The `-O` option is not POSIX-compliant, so we need to handle it differently.
# The `-P` option is not POSIX-compliant, so we need to handle it differently.
# The `-Q` option is not POSIX-compliant, so we need to handle it differently.
# The `-R` option is not POSIX-compliant, so we need to handle it differently.
